    "difficultyReason": "The first move is already worked: n^-1 has been moved to the numerator. Part a needs only the matching move of m^-2 to the denominator. Part b repeats the same two moves on c^-3/d^-4, with the method signposted in the prompt. There is no brackets, coefficient or mixed-sign decision. It is slightly more than the fill-in reciprocal in p10-q2, because the student must carry out a two-step move with little support in part b. It is below p8-q1, which asks the student to explain why the sign disappears and why the 3 stays, in addition to simplifying.",
